  "review": {
    "book": "2SA",
    "entityID": "person:ahithophel_162",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA15:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Absalom sent for Ahithophel the Gilonite, David’s counselor, from his city, even from Giloh, while he was offering the sacrifices. The conspiracy was strong, for the people increased continually with Absalom."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA15:31",
        "textualBasisJa": "Someone told David, saying, “Ahithophel is among the conspirators with Absalom.” David said, “LORD, please turn the counsel of Ahithophel into foolishness.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA15:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "but if you return to the city, and tell Absalom, ‘I will be your servant, O king. As I have been your father’s servant in time past, so I will now be your servant; then you will defeat for me the counsel of Ahithophel.’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Absalom and all the people, the men of Israel, came to Jerusalem, and Ahithophel with him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Absalom said to Ahithophel, “Give your counsel what we shall do.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ahithophel said to Absalom, “Go in to your father’s concubines that he has left to keep the house. Then all Israel will hear that you are abhorred by your father. Then the hands of all who are with you will be strong.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "The counsel of Ahithophel, which he gave in those days, was as if a man inquired at the inner sanctuary of God. All the counsel of Ahithophel was like this both with David and with Absalom."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moreover Ahithophel said to Absalom, “Let me now choose twelve thousand men, and I will arise and pursue after David tonight."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Hushai had come to Absalom, Absalom spoke to him, saying, “Ahithophel has spoken like this. Shall we do what he says? If not, speak up.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hushai said to Absalom, “The counsel that Ahithophel has given this time is not good.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Absalom and all the men of Israel said, “The counsel of Hushai the Archite is better than the counsel of Ahithophel.” For the LORD had ordained to defeat the good counsel of Ahithophel, to the intent that the LORD might bring evil on Absalom."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Hushai said to Zadok and to Abiathar the priests, “Ahithophel counseled Absalom and the elders of Israel that way; and I have counseled this way."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "After they had departed, they came up out of the well and went and told King David; and they said to David, “Arise and pass quickly over the water; for thus has Ahithophel counseled against you.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Ahithophel saw that his counsel was not followed, he saddled his donkey, arose, and went home to his city, set his house in order, and hanged himself; and he died, and was buried in the tomb of his father."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA23:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "Eliphelet the son of Ahasbai, the son of the Maacathite, Eliam the son of Ahithophel the Gilonite,"
      }
    ],
